 You must reside in Canada ; 
 You hold a Master's degree in mental health or a related field;  
 You are perfectly bilingual and fluent French and English, both verbally and in writing;  
 You are comfortable with technology (video calls, chat, emails, etc.);  
 You have experience with crisis management, risk assessment and risk management;  
 You can remain calm and in control, even in stressful or ambiguous situations;  
 You demonstrate sound clinical judgment and are able to quickly assess situations, identify an intervention goal, and support clients using a brief and strength-based approach;  
 You are empathetic, have good listening skills, and demonstrate e xcellent communication skills; 
 You can provide excellent customer service, manage client expectations, and respond effectively to their needs;  
 You are proactive, independent, resourceful and open to feedback;  
 You thrive in a high volume and a fast pace environment;  
 You are available to work o vernight, from Sunday to Thursday OR Tuesday to Saturday, from 11pm to 7:30am (Eastern time), including holidays. 
